flow_id,  from_card_id,  to_card_id,    label,             sort_order, standalone
@pb_flow, @pb_draft,     @pb_review,    "Send to review",  1,          true
@pb_flow, @pb_draft,     @pb_published, "Publish",         2,          false
@pb_flow, @pb_draft,     @pb_archived,  "Archive",         3,          false
@pb_flow, @pb_review,    @pb_published, "Publish",         1,          true
@pb_flow, @pb_review,    @pb_draft,     "Back to draft",   2,          false
@pb_flow, @pb_review,    @pb_archived,  "Archive",         3,          false
@pb_flow, @pb_published, @pb_published, "Publish changes", 1,          true
@pb_flow, @pb_published, @pb_review,    "Send to review",  2,          false
@pb_flow, @pb_published, @pb_draft,     "Unpublish",       3,          false
@pb_flow, @pb_published, @pb_archived,  "Archive",         4,          false
@pb_flow, @pb_archived,  @pb_draft,     "Restore",         1,          true

-- The Pages screen lists the project's page tree; Draft and In review /
-- Published are on by default, Archived is a toggle away.
## table card | under=bundle_src
### rows
card_type_id,      parent_card_id, title,   layout, slug,  hotkey, sort_order, flow_ref, default_create_status, toggle_groups
$card_type.screen, parent,         "Pages", pages,  pages, w,      8,          @pb_flow, @pb_draft,             `[{"name":"phase_scope","operator":"or","mode":"multi","items":[{"name":"triage","label":"Draft","predicate":{"attr":"publish_status","op":"has_phase","values":["triage"]},"default_on":true},{"name":"active","label":"Live","predicate":{"attr":"publish_status","op":"has_phase","values":["active"]},"default_on":true},{"name":"terminal","label":"Archived","predicate":{"attr":"publish_status","op":"has_phase","values":["terminal"]},"default_on":false}]}]`

-- A starter site: a Home page (the root a portal points at) with one child.
-- Their bodies show what the builder expands: {{< children >}} lists the
-- page's child pages, {{< toc >}} the page's headings, {{< nav >}} the
-- whole site tree, and a ref: link ([text](ref:slug/path)) points at
-- another page. A placeholder in backticks is shown as written.
## table card | under=bundle_src | alias=pb_home
### rows
card_type_id,    parent_card_id, title,  slug, sort_order, publish_status, description
$card_type.page, parent,         "Home", ,     0,          @pb_draft,      `Welcome. This is the root page of the site: a portal points at it, and every page under it is published beneath it.

## In this site

{{< children >}}

See [Getting started](ref:getting-started) for how pages, statuses and portals fit together.`

## table card | under=pb_home
### rows
card_type_id,    parent_card_id, title,             slug,              sort_order, publish_status, description
$card_type.page, parent,         "Getting started", "getting-started", 10,         @pb_draft,      `{{< toc >}}

## Write

Each page is a card. Its child pages are its section, so the card tree is the site tree. A page's slug is its path segment.

## Review and publish

Move a page through its statuses. A status can publish to one or more portals: send a page to review and it appears on QA; publish it and it appears on QA and PROD.

## Live edits

Editing a published page doesn't change what a portal shows. Use **Publish changes** to send the edit out, or send the page back to review.

## Unpublish

**Unpublish** (or **Back to draft**) takes the page off every portal: a draft isn't live anywhere. **Archive** does the same and hides it from the Pages screen.

## Links and placeholders

Link to another page by giving the link the target ``ref:`` plus the page's path or number: [this link](ref:) goes to the home page, and ``ref:getting-started`` points at this one.

These placeholders are filled in when a site is built: ``{{< children >}}`` lists the page's child pages, ``{{< nav >}}`` the whole site, and ``{{< toc >}}`` the page's headings. In backticks, like here, they are shown as written.`
